-- title:
--   Existence of a canonical L-map for formal mathcal O_D-modules
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a commutative ring $B$ together with a ring homomorphism $j\colon \mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to B$ (the source being [`CerednikDrinfeld.Zp2 p`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalModule.html#L17), the Witt vectors of the field with $p^2$ elements), and assume $B$ is Hausdorff for the filtration by powers of the ideal generated by $p$. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$: a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $X.F$ equipped with an action of $\mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{p^2})$ by endomorphism power series and a uniformiser endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi = [p]$ and $\varpi\circ[a] = [\sigma a]\circ\varpi$. Let $\gamma\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to$ `CartierModule p X.F` be a homogeneous $V$-basis in the sense of the structure-constant module, i.e. each $\gamma_i$ lies in the $i$-th graded piece — the subgroup of curves $f$ with $[c]_*f = j(\tau(c))^{p^i}\cdot f$ for every Teichmüller element $\tau(c)$, $c\in\mathbb{F}_{p^2}$ — and the matrix of tangent coefficients $(\mathrm{tangent}(\gamma_i)_k)$ has unit determinant; assume moreover that the graded pieces in degrees $0$ and $1$ are complementary subgroups of the Cartier module, as recorded by `hc`. Write $D = X.$`toGradedCartierModuleData`$\,j\,hc$ for the resulting graded Cartier datum: the Cartier module of $X.F$ with its Frobenius, integral Verschiebung, the operator induced by $\varpi$, and the two graded submodules as $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$-pieces. The assertion is that there exists an additive map $L$ from $D.M$ to $D.$`NMod`, the quotient of $D.M \times D.\Sigma$ (where $\Sigma$ is $D.M$ with Witt-module structure twisted by Frobenius) by the relation $D.$`nRel`, which is canonical: $L$ is a Cartier $L$-map for $D$, and there are a commutative ring $S$ with $j_S\colon \mathbb{W}(\mathbb{F}_{p^2}) \to S$, a surjective ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon S \to B$, no $p$-torsion in $S$ (that is, $ps = 0$ implies $s = 0$), a graded Cartier datum $D_\ell$ over $S$ that is special (it admits a homogeneous $V$-basis and is $V$-adically complete), an additive map $f\colon D_\ell.M \to D.M$ which is a base change along $\varphi$, and a Cartier $L$-map $L_\ell$ for $D_\ell$, such that $L(f(x)) = D_\ell.$`nMap`$(L_\ell(x))$ for all $x \in D_\ell.M$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the construction of the canonical $L$-map attached to a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation, in the form of Boutot–Carayol II (3.8) applied to the concrete model $M = \mathrm{Hom}(\widehat{W}, X.F)$ rather than to abstract graded Cartier data. It feeds the rigidification of the base point and the construction of the Cartier quadruple, and is used by the variants for special modules over algebraically closed and reduced base rings.
